see "../src/harness.vox".
see "../src/runner.vox".
see "../src/findings.vox".

(FUZZER_DEFECTS.md defect 9 - the differential self-consistency oracle.
 Two claims, proven directly against the real capability rather than
 through the seed-based generator (which the 300-seed campaign already
 covers, and which by construction can never emit this fixture):

   1. 'run program capturing' really captures a fresh, comparable copy
      of stdout on each call - not the SAME file re-read, and not the
      fuzzer's own stdout.
   2. A save through 'finding save' - the same call loop_gen.vox now
      makes on a mismatch - keeps BOTH captured outputs in the finding,
      not just the fact that they differed. A finding without both is
      useless (the brief's own words); grep for both markers rather
      than the unpredictable pid values themselves, since those can
      never be pinned in a golden file.

 tests/fixtures/nondeterministic.vox is planted by hand: it prints raw
 /proc/self/stat, whose first field is the process's own pid - genuinely
 different on every fork/exec of the very same binary, the same "prints
 something that MOVES" shape bug #39 was before it was fixed in 0.4.7.)

Set findings_dir to "./vf_test_nondeterm_findings".
a number called 'the cleanup before' is 'run shell' of "rm -rf ./vf_test_nondeterm_findings ./vf_nd1 ./vf_nd2" and 5000.

a number called 'the compile result' is 'compile vox' of "." and "tests/fixtures/nondeterministic.vox" and "./vf_nd_bin" and "./vf_nd_cerr".
Print "compiled: {'the compile result' is 0}".

a text called 'run1 verdict' is 'run program capturing' of "./vf_nd_bin" and 5000 and "./vf_nd1".
a text called 'run2 verdict' is 'run program capturing' of "./vf_nd_bin" and 5000 and "./vf_nd2".
Print "both runs exited cleanly: {'run1 verdict' is 'run2 verdict'}".

a text called 'the first output' is 'read whole file' of "./vf_nd1".
a boolean called 'first read ok' is 'the last read succeeded'.
a text called 'the second output' is 'read whole file' of "./vf_nd2".
a boolean called 'second read ok' is 'the last read succeeded'.
Print "both captures readable: {'first read ok'} {'second read ok'}".

If 'the first output' is not 'the second output' then,
    Print "oracle sees the mismatch: true".
Otherwise,
    Print "oracle sees the mismatch: false".

a text called 'the mismatch detail' is "run 1: {'the first output'}\n---\nrun 2: {'the second output'}".
a number called 'the finding tally' is 'finding save' of "nondeterministic" and 900777 and "tests/fixtures/nondeterministic.vox" and 'the mismatch detail'.
Print "finding saved: {'the finding tally' is greater than 0}".

a number called 'the finding dir check' is 'run shell' of "test -d ./vf_test_nondeterm_findings/nondeterministic/900777" and 5000.
Print "finding directory exists: {'the finding dir check' is 0}".
a number called 'the run1 marker check' is 'run shell' of "grep -q 'run 1:' ./vf_test_nondeterm_findings/nondeterministic/900777/classification.txt" and 5000.
Print "classification has run 1 output: {'the run1 marker check' is 0}".
a number called 'the run2 marker check' is 'run shell' of "grep -q 'run 2:' ./vf_test_nondeterm_findings/nondeterministic/900777/classification.txt" and 5000.
Print "classification has run 2 output: {'the run2 marker check' is 0}".

a number called 'the cleanup after' is 'run shell' of "rm -rf ./vf_test_nondeterm_findings ./vf_nd1 ./vf_nd2 ./vf_nd_bin ./vf_nd_cerr" and 5000.
